 "text": "Hi, how have you been? No, it's much longer than that. A typical century is 60 miles or 120 kilometers. If you' reasonably fast, eight hours is about typical. If you stop for lunch, expect double that. It is. You need decent bike, plenty of time, and someone waiting for you at the finish. Great. Start with shorter rides first, though. Go for a ten mile ride and see how you feel. If your legs still feel good at the end, up it a little. Lots of base mileage first, then build up few slow miles a week before the big day. mix of terrain matters too, road builds your endurance, the trails build your skills.",
